nothing-playing = Nothing playing
nothing-playing-more = Play a track and the pane decodes it from end to end: its waveform, its spectrum, whether its lossless claim holds and what its audio is.
failed = This track couldn't be decoded
failed-more = The file may be truncated or damaged. The log says where the decoder stopped.
analysing = Decoding the whole track…
reads-hint = The whole track decoded once, off the audio thread. A lossy encode throws away what lies above a fixed frequency, so a lossless file made from one shows a wall in its spectrum where the encoder cut; an upsample shows the wall where the lower rate ended; padded bits are low bits that never move.
take-the-name = Take this name
nothing-to-take = The catalog holds no recognition of this track to take a name from
take-the-name-hint = Write the title, the artist and the recording the audio was heard as into the catalog in place of what the file names. The file itself is left as it is.
